  "query_preview": "..\nRidging conditions aloft will be conducive for warmer than \naverage temperatures persisting through Tuesday. While a mid-level\ndisturbance exists, it will likely be too dry to induce any \nprecipitation, although the isolated chance still exists, \nconfidence remains low regarding any increase of PoPs. \n\nSunday onward, Southwesterly flow aloft will cause a trough in \nthe upper-levels to form and a low pressure system upstream. This\nwill lead to water vapor transport from the Pacific Ocean, giving\nthe area the moisture and lift it needs for precipitation. How \nconditionally unstable the environment may be, will dictate \nprecipitation chances as well as timing of the passage of the \nweather system. GEFS and EPS are not in agreement after Monday, so\nwe will have to await further model guidance to confirm a range \nof possible QPF totals. It is setting up and presenting itself as\na multi-day rain event with potential impacts if it were to come \nto fruition, however, due to the spread of QPF, the timing, and \nplacement of the low, it's too soon to hone in on any QPF totals\nand subsequent impacts.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Confidence for fog development and placement is low (25%).\n \n- Confidence in warm and dry conditions persisting through Monday\n  PM is high (75%). \n\n- Confidence in mid-week trough timing is on the low end of\n  moderate (40%).\n\n- Confidence in LLWS potential at KGDV is moderate (50%). \n\n\nFINDLEY",
